<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Herodian Ethnarchy of Judea</h1><p class="st-meta">4 BCE – 6 CE · capital Jerusalem</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The short reign of Herod Archelaus over Judea, Samaria and Idumaea, whose failure led Rome to rule Judea directly through prefects.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great's</a> will named <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-archelaus">Archelaus</a> as heir to the kingship, but Augustus in 4 BCE gave him only the title ethnarch and the heartland of the kingdom: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaea">Judea</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idumaea">Idumaea</a>, about half of his father's territory, with the promise of a crown if he governed well.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>His reign began with the killing of some three thousand people when he suppressed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/passover">Passover</a> protest in the Temple courts, and further revolts had to be crushed by the Syrian governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-quinctilius-varus">Varus</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-archelaus">Archelaus</a> founded the village of Archelais, planted palms near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jericho">Jericho</a> and rebuilt the palace there. His marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glaphyra">Glaphyra</a>, widow of his half-brother, offended religious opinion.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 6 CE a joint delegation of Judeans and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaritans">Samaritans</a> complained to Augustus, who deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-archelaus">Archelaus</a> and exiled him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaea">Judea</a> became a Roman province under equestrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prefect">prefects</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/census">census</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/publius-sulpicius-quirinius">Quirinius</a> that followed provoked the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judas-of-galilee">Judas of Galilee</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="principality, 4 BCE – 6 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">principality</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:59.62%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>4 BCE – 6 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Jerusalem</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Herod Archelaus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Judaism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Aramaic, Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/israel">Israel</a>, <a href="/countries/palestine">Palestine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ethnarchy of Archelaus</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1&amp;focus=herodian-ethnarchy-of-judea" aria-label="Herodian Ethnarchy of Judea on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5588 1021 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Herodian Ethnarchy of Judea lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5908 1277L5908 1277M5908 1277L5304 942"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5908 1277h0M5304 942h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5908 1277h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5908 1277h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Jerusalem. <a href="/atlas?year=1&amp;focus=herodian-ethnarchy-of-judea">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
